title HUNK83 — the OR of clauses: widen the marketplace to the parts matching any facet
prompt continue the recursion after HUNK82; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve, send as its own signed round to origin and xykj61, stop at custody gates
think HUNK78 gave the marketplace a conjunction (narrow to the parts matching EVERY clause) — half of a real facet sidebar. The other half WIDENS: a keeper who checks two materials wants the union, the parts matching EITHER. By Lindy-first crux-first the durable next thing is completing the boolean query algebra — the dual of AND — so the marketplace runs on a whole algebra (narrow with AND, widen with OR), a primitive reused across every search.
think Chose image/part_or.rye mirroring part_and.rye clause for clause so the two read as the pair they are — parse_or into a bounded OrQuery (max_clauses = part_and.max_clauses so the superset check is measured at equal width), matches_any (matches with a logical OR, empty is false), count_or, filter_or over the same shared sheet. No new matching rule: a disjunction is just HUNK75's matches asked of every clause with OR.
think The crux is the union law: filter_or keeps exactly the parts passing at least one clause, each part once, in the catalog's held order. Two laws make the dual honest: the De Morgan identity (empty AND is match-all, empty OR is match-none — following the algebra rather than a friendlier guess keeps them true duals) and the superset relation (over the same clauses OR is a superset of AND — a free cross-check against HUNK78 on one catalog filtered both ways).
obs GREEN on the first build. Proven on metal over five parts across three materials and a price spread: material:stainless-304 material:brass keeps the two stainless parts each once; stainless OR max:10 keeps the union bolt/washer/hexnut with the membership reference confirming every kept part passes some clause and every dropped part none; the clauses commute (held order is the catalog's); a single clause behaves like the plain filter; an empty line is a match-none; OR is a superset of AND (stainless max:60 keeps hexnut alone under AND, four parts under OR — every AND match an OR match, and strictly wider here); a malformed clause (UnknownKey, NoColon) and an over-many line (TooManyClauses) refuse by name before any walk.
obs A price clause compares a recorded cent count, never moved (custody gate #3 untouched). No network, no key, no funds. TAME bans clean (not flagged by the scan), width exit 0; HUNK78 conjunction re-run GREEN beneath.
loom witness=hunk_part_or_witness parts=5 or_superset_of_and=true empty_or=match_none
